# Whitelist: the image consumes ONLY the staged per-arch slim trees.
# Everything else in the build context (node_modules, src, dist, the npm
# package staging) would bloat it by hundreds of MB and invalidate layer
# caching on every source edit.
#
# Named after the Dockerfile, not .dockerignore at the context root:
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile whatever the
# context, so the same whitelist holds for every image this file builds,
# including stigmer-server-ee, whose context is ee/server.
*
!dist-slim-amd64
!dist-slim-arm64
